.TH CHADDR-PROFILE 5 "June 2026" "chaddr @VERSION@" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
chaddr-profile \- chaddr address profile file format
.SH DESCRIPTION
A
.I chaddr
profile is a plain-text file that declares how to discover the current IP
addresses of a host and which resources must be checked or updated when those
addresses change. Profiles are read by
.BR chaddr (1).
.PP
Each file is a sequence of
.BR key: value
lines. Keys are case-insensitive. Empty lines and lines beginning with
.B #
are ignored, except for special
.B # option
directives (see below). A trailing backslash
.B \(rs
at the end of a physical line continues the line on the next line (shell-style
continuation).
.SH FILE LOCATION
Profile files have no required filename extension. By default they live in
.IR ~/.config/chaddr/profile/ .
Override the directory with the
.B CHADDR_PROFILE_DIR
environment variable. Example profiles ship in
.IR /usr/share/chaddr/profile/
when installed from a package, or in
.I profile/
in a source checkout. On first run, an empty user profile directory is seeded
from those examples.
.SH STRUCTURE
Profiles contain, in order:
.IP \(bu 3
An optional
.B header
(before the first
.B from:
or
.B type:
line).
.IP \(bu 3
An optional
.B from
block that resolves current addresses.
.IP \(bu 3
One or more
.B type
blocks, each describing a resource
.B chaddr
can diagnose, renew, or manually update.
.PP
A profile may contain multiple
.B type:
blocks. Each block starts with
.B type: \(laNAME\(ra
and continues until the next
.B type:
or
.B from:
line or end of file.
.SH HEADER
Header fields appear before the first
.B from:
or
.B type:
line.
.TP
.B description: \(laTEXT\(ra
Short human-readable label shown in the GUI profile list.
.TP
.B version: \(laTEXT\(ra
Optional version string shown in the GUI profile list.
.TP
.B history-addr: \(laADDR\(ra \(dq\(laINSERTTIME\(ra\(dq [\(dq\(laEVENTTIME\(ra\(dq]
Canonical historical address entry (may appear multiple times).
.I INSERTTIME
is when the record was added (quoted
.BR "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS" ).
.I EVENTTIME
is optional business time for the address.
These addresses are treated like spare
.BR \-\-old-ip
values when matching old IPs in
.BR hosts (5)
entries and BIND zone files during diagnose and apply.
.TP
.B addr-history: \(laADDR\(ra [\(laTIMESTAMP\(ra]
Legacy form (still read). One address per line with optional unquoted
timestamp, or a single line with multiple IPs. On save (renew or History tab),
legacy lines are rewritten as
.B history-addr
entries.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
history-addr: 198.51.100.4 "2026-06-24 12:00:00"
history-addr: 2001:db8::1 "2026-06-24 12:00:00" "2026-06-25 09:15:00"
.fi
.RE
.SH FROM BLOCK
The optional
.B from
block tells
.B chaddr
how to discover the current primary addresses for the profile.
.TP
.B from: resolve
Use DNS to resolve a hostname.
.TP
.B resolve: \(laHOSTNAME\(ra
Hostname to resolve. Aliases:
.BR host: ,
.BR name: .
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
from: resolve
resolve: relay.example.com
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B from: ec2 nic
Use public IPv4 address(es) on a specific Elastic Network Interface (ENI).
Prefer this when the instance has multiple NICs. Renew keeps the association
on the same private address slot (primary or secondary) of that NIC.
Requires a matching
.B aws elastic ip
resource block in the same profile (for
.BR region: ).
.TP
.B nic: \(laENI-ID\(ra
.TP
.B eni: \(laENI-ID\(ra
.TP
.B network_interface: \(laENI-ID\(ra
ENI id for
.B from: ec2 nic
/
.BR "from: aliyun nic" .
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
from: ec2 nic
nic: eni-0123456789abcdef0
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B from: ec2
.TQ
.B from: ec2 instance
Discover public IPv4 addresses on an EC2 instance (every NIC). Renew only
reallocates public IPs that also appear in profile
.B history-addr
/
.B addr-history
(or GUI spare/old-ip). Unmatched public IPs on other ENIs are left alone.
Prefer
.B from: ec2 nic
when targeting a single NIC.
Requires a matching
.B aws elastic ip
resource block (for
.BR region: ).
.TP
.B from: aliyun
.TQ
.B from: aliyun instance
Use the public IPv4 of an Aliyun ECS instance as a from-source address.
Requires a matching
.B aliyun elastic ip
resource block (for
.BR region: ).
.TP
.B from: aliyun nic
Aliyun ENI-scoped from-source (same
.B nic:
keys as
.BR "from: ec2 nic" ).
.TP
.B instance: \(laID\(ra
.TP
.B instance_id: \(laID\(ra
EC2 or ECS instance ID. When omitted (and no
.B nic:
is set), the cloud handler searches running instances in the configured region.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
from: ec2
instance: i-0123456789abcdef0
.fi
.RE
.PP
GUI address sources use the short labels
.BR ec2 ,
.BR "ec2 nic" ,
.BR aliyun ,
and
.BR "aliyun nic"
(not a generic
.BR instance
label).
.B from: ec2 instance
is accepted as an alias of
.BR "from: ec2" ;
.B from: aliyun instance
aliases
.BR "from: aliyun" .
.SH CLI OPTIONS IN PROFILES
Lines of the form:
.PP
.RS
.B # option \-\-flag
.RE
.PP
attach extra CLI flags to the following
.B type:
block. At the very beginning of a file (before any header,
.B from:
or
.B type:
line), such lines register global CLI options for the profile.
.PP
Credentials and secrets are normally read from
.IR chaddr.conf ;
profile
.B # option
lines are mainly for per-block flags required by handlers.
.SH RESOURCE TYPES
Each resource block begins with
.B type: \(laNAME\(ra
where
.I NAME
is one of the supported types below (case-insensitive).
.PP
Any type block may include
.B optional: true
(also
.BR yes ,
.BR on ,
or
.BR 1 ).
In the GUI Instructions tab such blocks start deselected; the CLI still runs
them unless an instruction filter is applied.
.SS aws elastic ip
Diagnose and renew (reallocate) an AWS Elastic IP associated with an EC2
instance.
.TP
.B region: \(laREGION\(ra
AWS region ID or short alias. Aliases include
.IR sg1 ,
.IR kr1 ,
.IR hk1 ,
.IR jp1 ,
.IR jp2 ,
.IR au1 ,
.IR us1 ,
and
.IR us2 .
.TP
.B instance: \(laID\(ra
.TP
.B instance_id: \(laID\(ra
Optional EC2 instance ID. When omitted, the handler searches running instances
in the configured region.
.PP
Requires AWS credentials in
.IR chaddr.conf .
.SS aliyun elastic ip
Diagnose and renew (reallocate) an Aliyun Elastic IP.
.TP
.B region: \(laREGION\(ra
Aliyun region ID or alias (
.IR cn1 ,
.IR cn2 ,
.IR cn3 ,
.IR sg1 ,
.IR hk1 ,
etc.).
.TP
.B instance: \(laID\(ra
.TP
.B instance_id: \(laID\(ra
Optional ECS instance ID. When omitted, the handler searches running instances.
.PP
Requires Aliyun credentials in
.IR chaddr.conf .
.SS registered nameserver
Diagnose and manually apply IP changes to registered nameservers (Namecheap).
.TP
.B api: namecheap
Namecheap API (required).
.TP
.B ns: \(laHOSTS\(ra
Comma-separated nameserver hostnames, for example
.IR ns1.example.com ,
.IR ns2.example.com .
.TP
.B domain: \(laDOMAIN\(ra
.TP
.B ns_domain: \(laDOMAIN\(ra
Optional parent domain. When omitted, the domain is derived from the first
nameserver hostname.
.PP
Apply sets each configured nameserver glue record to the selected new IPv4.
The profile
.B from:
address map is not used to match current glue IPs; only the
.B ns:
hostnames matter.
.PP
Requires Namecheap API credentials in
.IR chaddr.conf .
.SS hosts file
Diagnose and manually apply IP changes in a local
.BR hosts (5)
file.
.TP
.B path: \(laFILE\(ra
Path to the hosts file (for example
.IR /etc/hosts ).
.TP
.B host: \(laNAMES\(ra
.TP
.B hosts: \(laNAMES\(ra
Optional comma-separated hostnames to limit which lines are considered. When
omitted, all lines matching spare/old IP addresses are updated.
.SS zone file
Diagnose and manually apply IP changes in a BIND zone file.
The legacy type name
.B bind db
is still accepted.
.TP
.B path: \(laFILE\(ra
Path to the zone database file.
.TP
.B record: \(laNAMES\(ra
.TP
.B name: \(laNAMES\(ra
Optional comma-separated record names to limit which A records are updated.
.SS file
Diagnose and manually apply IP changes in a plain-text file (for example
Makefiles, config snippets, or sources list files).
.TP
.B path: \(laFILE\(ra
Path to the file.
.PP
IPv4 and IPv6 literals are matched with alphanumeric lookbehind/lookahead
(not word boundaries), so dotted addresses inside longer tokens are not
matched. Spare/old IP candidates from
.B history-addr
/
.B addr-history ,
.B from:
blocks, and
.B \-\-old-ip
determine which literals to replace.
.SS changelog
Append a Debian-style changelog entry when an IP address is applied.
.TP
.B path: \(laFILE\(ra
Path to the
.I debian/changelog
file.
.PP
Shorthand form is also accepted:
.PP
.RS
.B changelog: \(laFILE\(ra
.RE
.PP
On apply, the handler bumps the last numeric component of the top version,
reuses the previous distribution name (falling back past
.B UNRELEASED
when needed), keeps the previous author trailer, and inserts a new entry:
.PP
.RS
.nf
package (1.0.106) testing; urgency=medium

  * chaddr IPv4 from <old> to <new>

 -- Author Name <email>  Day, DD Mon YYYY HH:MM:SS +ZZZZ
.fi
.RE
.SS router
Diagnose and manually apply IP changes to a LAN router over SSH.
Currently supports OpenWrt UCI updates for Shadowsocks remote server
addresses.
.TP
.B system: openwrt
Router OS (required; only
.B openwrt
is supported).
.TP
.B config: shadowsocks remote server
Update UCI
.B server
sections under
.I shadowsocks-libev
or
.IR shadowsocks .
.TP
.B user: \(laNAME\(ra
SSH username (default
.BR root ).
.TP
.B password: \(laSECRET\(ra
SSH password. May instead be supplied as
.B router_password
in
.IR chaddr.conf .
.TP
.B host: \(laADDR\(ra
.TP
.B gateway: \(laADDR\(ra
Optional router address. When omitted, the IPv4 default gateway from
.I /proc/net/route
is used.
.TP
.B port: \(laN\(ra
.TP
.B ssh_port: \(laN\(ra
Optional SSH port (default
.BR 22 ).
.TP
.B optional: true
When set, the instruction is listed in the GUI Instructions tab but
deselected by default (CLI still runs it unless filtered).
.PP
Requires
.B python3-paramiko
for SSH.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
type: router
optional: true
system: openwrt
user: root
password: secret
config: shadowsocks remote server
.fi
.RE
.SH ACTIONS BY TYPE
.TP
.B Diagnose
All supported types.
.TP
.B Renew (reallocate)
.B aws elastic ip
and
.B aliyun elastic ip
only.
.TP
.B Apply (manual IP change)
.B registered nameserver ,
.BR hosts file ,
.BR zone file ,
.BR file ,
.BR changelog ,
and
.BR router .
.SH EXAMPLE
.PP
.RS
.nf
# chaddr example profile
description: Example relay
version: 1
history-addr: 198.51.100.4 "2026-06-24 12:00:00"
history-addr: 2001:db8::1 "2026-06-24 12:00:00"
history-addr: 203.0.113.10 "2026-06-25 09:15:00"

from: resolve
resolve: relay.example.com

type: aws elastic ip
region: us-east-1

type: aliyun elastic ip
region: cn-hangzhou

type: registered nameserver
api: namecheap
ns: ns1.example.com, \\
   ns2.example.com

type: hosts file
path: /etc/hosts

type: zone file
path: /var/cache/bind/db.example.com

type: router
optional: true
system: openwrt
user: root
password: secret
config: shadowsocks remote server
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chaddr (1),
.BR hosts (5),
.BR named (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Lenik &lt;chaddr@bodz.net&gt;
